     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Menhet|400663\", \"verdict\": \"different_name\", \"reasoning\": \"Record 2 reads j, m, n, y, w, ꜣ, ḥ, w. In Menhet, M matches m. The e after it can stand for no sign. N matches n. The e between n and h can stand for ꜣ, with the j, y and w left out, which is allowed. H matches ḥ, and the final w can also be left out. The final t of Menhet has no sign to represent it. The transliteration ends in w, not in a feminine t, and the rule only lets a t be left out of record 1's spelling, not added. That leaves a consonant in record 1 that the transliteration lacks, so the names differ.\"}"
     }
